{
 "about": "Synthetic demo for the CTM console: Leo works in Claude Code, Ali in Codex. Made by node demo/console-recording.mjs from demo/leo-orbit.jsonl and demo/ali-orbit.jsonl with the real store; every name and plan is made up.",
 "durationMs": 34000,
 "sessions": {
  "81c09658b44b9afe2523ce0b5ad6efc036de5a4d40db9802315754ca80fe691a": {
   "id": "81c09658b44b9afe2523ce0b5ad6efc036de5a4d40db9802315754ca80fe691a",
   "provider": "claude",
   "source": "leo-orbit.jsonl",
   "title": "We are demoing Orbit at the hackathon. The goal: the Orbit demo is live by 19:00 on Saturday.",
   "messageCount": 56,
   "project": "default",
   "messages": [
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "We are demoing Orbit at the hackathon. The goal: the Orbit demo is live by 19:00 on Saturday.",
     "line": 1,
     "key": "h:e94d48b33f27c0e65e730f07ed95dbe8"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Understood. The goal is the Orbit demo live by 19:00 on Saturday. I will keep a list of decisions as we go.",
     "line": 2,
     "key": "h:ddd54503d8c2e2e5164894effbb66a0a"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Run the ledger on port 4400 for the demo.",
     "line": 3,
     "key": "h:1d8c6d5c110304902a5065efc8e10fab"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Decision recorded: the ledger runs on port 4400 for the demo.",
     "line": 4,
     "key": "h:21419622326c3dd804bdc3b0b8ab5988"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "The slide title font looks heavy on the projector. Can we try something lighter?",
     "line": 5,
     "key": "h:abf5d754c79016579e95d4e81cc47045"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Switched the deck to a lighter weight and bumped the line height. The title now fits on one line at 1280 pixels wide, and the speaker notes are unchanged.",
     "line": 6,
     "key": "h:767ca5019fb4876827b612c1e3b9770e"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "The room test flaked again on the second run. Look at it before we change anything else.",
     "line": 7,
     "key": "h:8d5786e28cdba22791ade1db54c67122"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "The flake came from a test that reused the database file between runs. Each run now gets its own temporary folder and the test passed ten times in a row.",
     "line": 8,
     "key": "h:347a667e0f697846b1e22210e1cbd7b8"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Remind me what the savings meter actually counts.",
     "line": 9,
     "key": "h:abee3f05011f6f821cf5d64f4119c46c"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "It counts UTF-16 code units divided by four for both the full handoff and the graph context, and it labels the numbers as estimates because tokenizers differ by vendor.",
     "line": 10,
     "key": "h:6c61abf9ee2955762cb60e4401a7996f"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Plan to record the demo video on Sunday morning.",
     "line": 11,
     "key": "h:35299a976df3020e7113a8899097a4fe"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Added an action: record the demo video on Sunday morning.",
     "line": 12,
     "key": "h:701874c9877fe20e873444c81f4b6027"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Is the browser view readable on a small screen?",
     "line": 13,
     "key": "h:d7237d70f5bc13d2799bb6923360f14e"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "At 375 pixels the room view stacks the two parties vertically and every button stays reachable. The proposal list scrolls inside its card.",
     "line": 14,
     "key": "h:b4b36e858738e3f490fce5380d7783fa"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Lunch is at 13:00, I will be away for forty minutes.",
     "line": 15,
     "key": "h:5799ece6f67247ff99fd9bb72079bf5a"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Noted. I will keep going on the README section while you are away and will not push anything.",
     "line": 16,
     "key": "h:cddd9490b31fd332923ee1148ccf1397"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Can you tidy the README intro? It reads like a spec.",
     "line": 17,
     "key": "h:ff8013194db0450f488d1af06bb69e23"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Rewrote the intro as two short paragraphs: what the ledger does and how two agents use it. The command reference moved below.",
     "line": 18,
     "key": "h:f837b3844c84a8fded50301962346c43"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Why does the context put actions last?",
     "line": 19,
     "key": "h:559a224a365444136844c7726000ed3b"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Stable sections go first so the prefix stays byte-identical across revisions and providers can cache it. Statuses change often, so actions, blockers and questions come last.",
     "line": 20,
     "key": "h:9764d37cc31b911556d07927ed206a92"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "I can pair with Ali on the MCP adapter, that is my offer to him.",
     "line": 21,
     "key": "h:ab93bf7e16f8f1a0e945d89183fd1f78"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Noted your offer to Ali: you will pair with him on the MCP adapter.",
     "line": 22,
     "key": "h:997b74d0a8c3671aadbd894d1601ae49"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "The CI run on Linux took eleven minutes. Is that normal?",
     "line": 23,
     "key": "h:aad9f97a72305c3b2286a9b728cdbcb5"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Most of it is the Playwright browser download. Caching the browser folder would save around six minutes, which is worth doing after the demo.",
     "line": 24,
     "key": "h:a58b7a64985872009132dc2e8a20cf28"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Check the escaping of labels with odd Unicode.",
     "line": 25,
     "key": "h:ce77a2b35ec0052c410f4cd6672f1b39"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Labels with line separators, bidi controls or control characters are escaped onto one line. I added a test with a right-to-left override and it renders as an escape.",
     "line": 26,
     "key": "h:d2c5b3b7366fe844f6ed481ac2472809"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Port 4400 clashes with Ali's Grafana. Change of plan: the ledger stays on port 4317.",
     "line": 27,
     "key": "h:61c9cb1d0cc7d990dc9562e566cf0968"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Decision updated: the ledger stays on port 4317. This supersedes the earlier choice of port 4400.",
     "line": 28,
     "key": "h:819d19acf82775bb654d401be4ba48cb"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "What happens if both of us publish the same packet twice?",
     "line": 29,
     "key": "h:0bfb7f1d505e627afc97602e161691cf"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "An exact repeat returns the same graph ID, so nothing is duplicated. A changed packet gets a new ID and needs a new room.",
     "line": 30,
     "key": "h:8534ea5b6f9aeb5420fe120ebb1d4f2f"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "The colour of the reject button is too close to the confirm button.",
     "line": 31,
     "key": "h:1c8eda87135ec6a81b094bc767ce2726"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Reject now uses the outline style and confirm the filled style. Both pass the contrast check in light and dark mode.",
     "line": 32,
     "key": "h:a44357f20a2e92bea693eaef96771054"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Do we need to mention the latent pool in the demo?",
     "line": 33,
     "key": "h:20e6def8b72709c3c59bc50485049e34"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Only as a closing slide. The two-agent room is the main story and the latent pool needs the GPU box, which may not be on stage.",
     "line": 34,
     "key": "h:0f234566ba4bf6b622aca896cabfdb20"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Stage Wi-Fi was flaky at the last event. Everything must run on the local laptop, not over stage Wi-Fi.",
     "line": 35,
     "key": "h:187551e142fccbe0bc1e7f3ab57ae732"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Constraint recorded: everything runs on the local laptop and nothing depends on stage Wi-Fi.",
     "line": 36,
     "key": "h:142ed4f321588ea540c96d91c0b3c517"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "The judges get five minutes per team.",
     "line": 37,
     "key": "h:cbb6f783dcedc284647f258929b903e0"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Then the live part should take three minutes at most, with a recorded fallback ready if the network or a CLI misbehaves.",
     "line": 38,
     "key": "h:50e4c8ff7e5d03811db838ad21bd2057"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Can the room survive a page reload?",
     "line": 39,
     "key": "h:ccf7a522fa585aff144658c4a13e04b7"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Yes. The address bar keeps the room ID after the hash sign, so a reload reopens the same room with the same choices.",
     "line": 40,
     "key": "h:e3c174174af72a8eee0c047a9a0b0b33"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Ali said he cannot work on Sunday. Move the recording to Saturday at 17:00.",
     "line": 41,
     "key": "h:0a2d4aa392c15b90dea5ef787c1f8c75"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Moved the action: record the demo video on Saturday at 17:00, two hours before the deadline. The Sunday plan is dropped.",
     "line": 42,
     "key": "h:a055f2b0c533c5d2000872a21235632d"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Write down the risks for the demo.",
     "line": 43,
     "key": "h:9c33da55bc61627406833130dec0d9c7"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Main risks: a CLI asking for login on stage, the tunnel dropping between laptops, and a model taking longer than expected. Each has a fallback in the run sheet.",
     "line": 44,
     "key": "h:872dc223d1be9d97c13f77c4c5d82e5e"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "How long does a publish take?",
     "line": 45,
     "key": "h:6313455c044b2f7427d7b1a4b0c9dad3"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Under twenty milliseconds on this laptop for a graph with a dozen nodes. Validation and hashing dominate, and the database write is small.",
     "line": 46,
     "key": "h:f727f969c8852b281e97c21691dadda1"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "The slide title font looks heavy on the projector. Can we try something lighter?",
     "line": 47,
     "key": "h:513c35c29c65775714520e07f4b6f987"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Switched the deck to a lighter weight and bumped the line height. The title now fits on one line at 1280 pixels wide, and the speaker notes are unchanged.",
     "line": 48,
     "key": "h:5a1351f2f09ead0b6233203d726e8fd6"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Is the browser view readable on a small screen?",
     "line": 49,
     "key": "h:d22829d8a87139c9606996c920a19f5b"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "At 375 pixels the room view stacks the two parties vertically and every button stays reachable. The proposal list scrolls inside its card.",
     "line": 50,
     "key": "h:8f80ff34cfa8cb9168d22457fbc30e09"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "One thing I still need from Ali: who owns the GPU box?",
     "line": 51,
     "key": "h:d167c9868d7d638fbb1db17ec0f4fc3c"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Open question for Ali: who owns the GPU box? I will leave it open until he answers.",
     "line": 52,
     "key": "h:5cae0eef3088cd687499d7edddd7f385"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "Why does the context put actions last?",
     "line": 53,
     "key": "h:4c58c3d1b279ff4a3c68497816e155d2"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "Stable sections go first so the prefix stays byte-identical across revisions and providers can cache it. Statuses change often, so actions, blockers and questions come last.",
     "line": 54,
     "key": "h:3e7f4a4ada13efa188c8a77a4338d5cd"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "What happens if both of us publish the same packet twice?",
     "line": 55,
     "key": "h:f1ae2708e32aacee6cc2bfab4bef122a"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "An exact repeat returns the same graph ID, so nothing is duplicated. A changed packet gets a new ID and needs a new room.",
     "line": 56,
     "key": "h:233d6ba05980f0de7f8ecb93fe008420"
    }
   ]
  },
  "2e5bf8a1c38d65bc260d6d618bac3e05876f02324c6b74e31514b623b2c36969": {
